    "intro_narrative": "You stand in the dimly lit office of Arthur Penhaligon, a private investigator who vanished without a trace exactly one week ago. The air is thick with the smell of stale tobacco and old paper. The door has firmly locked behind you, sealing you inside this paranoid man's sanctuary. Scattered across the mahogany desk and hidden in the shadows are various bizarre cryptographic devices, mechanical rings, and an ominous master terminal blinking in the center of the room. Penhaligon was on the verge of uncovering a massive conspiracy, and he hid his final conclusion behind layers of complex, interlocking puzzles. Your objective is clear: navigate his convoluted web of clues, decipher the hidden message, and unlock the master terminal to escape with the truth. The clock is ticking, and whoever took Arthur might be coming back.",
    "narrative_style": "mystery"
  },
